WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
professor Dave here, let's learn about
chemical bonds

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.960
a molecule is made up of atoms that are participating in chemical
bonds with one another. there are

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.630
different types of bonds that we will
want to be able to describe and the key

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:21.100
to their formation has to do with the
difference in electronegativity between

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:25.680
the two atoms participating in the bond.
if the difference is more than about 2

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:30.340
like with sodium and chlorine, chlorine
will steal an electron from sodium

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:35.059
chlorine really wants another electron,
sodium really wants to get rid of one so

00:00:35.059 --> 00:00:40.050
everybody wins. the result is a
positively charged sodium ion and a

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:44.670
negatively charged chloride ion.
particles of opposite charge have an

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:48.989
electrostatic attraction so these two
ions hang out together by forming an

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:53.350
ionic bond. this is a very strong
attraction because it is happening

00:00:53.350 --> 00:01:01.059
between ions that have a formal charge.
bond, ionic bond. electrons taken not

00:01:01.059 --> 00:01:04.850
shared. speaking of shared electrons if
the difference in electronegativity

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:11.320
between the two atoms is less than about
1.7 no electrons are stolen but instead

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:16.340
the two atoms share two electrons. the
electron from this atom feels the

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:20.549
attraction from the other nucleus and so
does the electron from this atom, so the

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:26.330
atoms share the two electrons to form a
covalent bond. covalent bonds can be

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:30.229
polar or nonpolar. if the
electronegativity difference between the

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:34.680
atoms is not high enough to cause
ionization but is at least more than

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.960
0.5, like with hydrogen and chlorine,
instead of completely stealing the

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:43.990
electron the chlorine will just sort of
hog the electrons in the resulting

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:48.799
covalent bond. the more electronegative
atom in a polar covalent bond pulls the

00:01:48.799 --> 00:01:53.939
electron density towards itself and as a
result of the slight electron excess we

00:01:53.939 --> 00:01:58.829
call this atom partially negative,
denoted by the symbol Delta minus. the

00:01:58.829 --> 00:02:03.710
atom whose electron is getting pulled
away is slightly electron deficient and

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:08.560
therefore partially positive or Delta
plus. if the electronegativity difference

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.760
is less than 0.5 the covalent bond is said to be

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:18.099
non polar. in a nonpolar covalent bond the
electrons are shared more or less evenly

00:02:18.099 --> 00:02:23.569
or in the case of two atoms of the same
element, precisely evenly. the atoms will

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:27.610
have no partial charges at all. other
than strange phenomena like metallic

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:31.290
bonding these are the main ways atoms
bind to one another

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:34.690
remember that you can predict the type
of bond that will form between two

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:39.510
elements by comparing their
electronegativites. if the difference

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:45.180
is very low, less than 0.5 or so, it will be
a nonpolar covalent bond where the

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:51.060
electrons are shared evenly. between
about 0.5 and 1.7 it'll be a polar

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:55.090
covalent bond with the electrons are
shared but one atom holds them more

00:02:55.090 --> 00:03:00.489
tightly. if above 2 or so one atom
will simply steal an electron from the

00:03:00.489 --> 00:03:05.359
other and you'll get ions that are
joined by on ionic bond. thanks for

00:03:05.359 --> 00:03:09.269
watching guys, subscribe to my channel
for more tutorials and as always feel

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:10.009
free to email me

